## Purpose

Implement durable recipient-owned contact grants/capabilities using the post-refactor persistence architecture.

## Work

- Add the reviewed capability/grant data model and backend operations with in-memory/SQLite parity.
- Implement cryptographically secure generation and constant-time validation where secret comparison applies.
- Enforce recipient/sender/relay scoping, expiry, revocation, rotation, uniqueness, and atomic one-time/replay semantics required by the design.
- Redact capability secrets from listings, logs, metrics, errors, registration leases, room metadata, and ordinary diagnostics.
- Add safe schema migration, rolling-upgrade handling, rollback considerations, and startup validation; never silently downgrade to default-allow.
- Add owner-authenticated management surfaces needed to issue, inspect safely, revoke, and rotate grants.

## Acceptance evidence

- Backend parity and migration tests pass with two-thread limits.
- Restart/persistence, concurrency, expiry, revocation, rollback, secret-redaction, and malformed-record tests pass.
- Key/capability material has explicit file/database access controls and no `show` command prints reusable secrets by default.